1
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:33,220
You're the only beat that's left.

2
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:44,340
You're the only beat that's left.

3
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:47,357
You're

4
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:53,937
the only beat that's left.

5
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:57,617
I don't see the rain on me.

6
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:01,140
I'm going to walk away.

7
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:06,577
The same thing I can see.

8
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:08,297
I'm just a mirror.

9
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:11,497
I'm not gonna walk away.

10
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:12,960
I love the world.

11
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:15,757
I love the world.

12
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:19,157
I love

13
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:24,000
the world.

14
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,660
If you want to run away, you'll be
able to catch up with the next day.

15
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:36,580
Come on, come on, come on, You'll
see everything in your eyes.

16
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:41,540
I'll show you in a dark heart.

17
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:46,040
Brand new world, start me up.

18
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:57,100
But he was CP9,

19
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:00,737
and the agents they have now are the
strongest the world has ever seen.

20
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:03,260
Even among them, Rob Lucci was the best.

21
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,800
These pirates are too powerful!

22
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,400
He won!

23
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:26,900
Luffy won!

24
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:44,860
Luffy, you had his words.

25
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:47,500
You finally beat him. Way to go!

26
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:48,870
Luffy!

27
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:53,417
Everybody head to the escape ship!

28
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,029
We're getting out of here!

29
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:57,480
He did it!

30
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:03,480
Way to go, Straw Hat!

31
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:06,900
Your corons keep it down!

32
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:09,340
Everyone can hear us! Who cares?

33
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:10,800
We want him to know!

34
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,940
Hey, those voices,
whose are they? Unknown!

35
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:17,057
They're coming in from somewhere
through a transponder snail, sir!

36
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:18,420
All right, big bro!

37
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,110
What?

38
00:03:27,193 --> 00:03:28,100
That voice!

39
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:40,460
Stop it! Huh?

40
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:43,057
They still think we're dead, remember?

41
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:45,300
You're gonna blow it! It's them.

42
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:47,600
They made it.

43
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:55,317
Aren't those the pirates we shot
down on the shore by the front gate?

44
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:58,220
It sounds like it, but sir, we saw them.

45
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:00,057
They all fell over the cliff, sir.

46
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:01,787
They couldn't have survived.

47
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:12,620
Big bro!

48
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:46,680
Oh, my God.

49
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:52,180
Stop pushing, you idiot!

50
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:54,640
We're gonna fall!

51
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:56,380
The rope's gonna break!

52
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:57,820
You morons!

53
00:04:57,980 --> 00:05:00,460
Galley-La robes never break! Calm down!

54
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:04,160
Geez, I told you to keep it quiet!

55
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,440
We're all okay!

56
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:08,620
Everybody made it! That
was close! The Giants!

57
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:11,560
They took all the cannon
fire for us! Get up!

58
00:05:11,940 --> 00:05:14,058
Gosh, they're a stubborn bunch, huh?

59
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,430
Uh-huh!

60
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:17,900
But hey, at least they're alive! Yeah!

61
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:20,700
Sodom and Gomorrah are okay, too!

62
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:22,240
That's great!

63
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:24,600
Look, it's not safe here.

64
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:26,677
Those battleships will be coming back.

65
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:28,177
We need to get moving now.

66
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:29,217
Right, listen up!

67
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:31,437
We got our escape plan all figured out.

68
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:32,350
Go!

69
00:05:32,433 --> 00:05:33,263
Don't worry about us!

70
00:05:33,346 --> 00:05:34,877
Let's all leave this place alive!

71
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:36,057
See you again soon!

72
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:37,140
Time to head out!

73
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:38,650
Move it!

74
00:05:38,733 --> 00:05:40,140
You guys climb up first!

75
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:42,940
Hurry up, Blood. Rushing to head.

76
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:44,420
Getting dizzy.

77
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:47,040
All right, climb!

78
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:50,020
Come on, everybody, get moving!

79
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:52,040
I'm gonna fall! Get off!

80
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,120
Stop shoving!

81
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:56,640
You dummies!

82
00:05:56,940 --> 00:06:00,860
I wasn't worried about you at all!

83
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:03,960
They made it, they're alive!

84
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:06,480
I'm so happy those idiots are okay!

85
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:12,340
Agreed. Good for them.

86
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,278
What a relief, huh?

87
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:17,136
But if you die here, it won't matter.

88
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:20,060
Yeah, you're right.

89
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:23,989
Sir, should we hurry
over to the main gate?

90
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:25,280
No, later.

91
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:26,840
First things first.

92
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:29,000
What's wrong? Move it.

93
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:31,180
We've got a duty to carry out.

94
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:32,530
Sir!

95
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:38,940
Bring it on!

96
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,591
I'll take all of you out!

97
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:48,540
I got trapped!

98
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:50,670
Onigiri!

99
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:52,410
Convenient!

100
00:06:58,200 --> 00:06:59,120
All right.

101
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:00,440
Snow Ball.

102
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:09,780
Our target is Straw Hat.

103
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:11,277
He's on the first column.

104
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:14,060
Right. Understood, sir. But he's... Hmm?

105
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:17,000
He doesn't seem to be moving!

106
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:19,197
Straw Hat Luffy is...

107
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:20,157
Sir, he...

108
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,240
He appears to be severely wounded!

109
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,430
What?

110
00:07:33,060 --> 00:07:33,890
Luffy!

111
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:36,000
What are you doing?

112
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:38,620
Hurry up and get the hell over here!

113
00:07:38,860 --> 00:07:41,213
If we don't escape, we're all gonna die!

114
00:07:47,060 --> 00:07:48,817
What's wrong with you damn it?

115
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:50,300
We're almost there!

116
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:53,377
Use your powers to slingshot
yourself over here!

117
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:55,519
I'll carry you the rest of the way!

118
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:03,680
We're surrounded by Snow
battleships on all sides!

119
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:06,097
If we stay here, we're gonna be killed!

120
00:08:06,180 --> 00:08:10,180
It seems the pirates planned to
escape using the stolen escort ship.

121
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,260
Luffy!

122
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:22,100
I can't.

123
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,760
My body won't. What?

124
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:36,080
My body won't move.

125
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:37,920
It won't move?

126
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:40,640
Come on, don't be stupid!

127
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:42,960
You just beat Luchi, didn't you?

128
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,040
And we already saved Robin!

129
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:47,301
The only thing left to do is run!

130
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:48,680
Try harder!

131
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:50,080
You can do it!

132
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:58,350
Usum!

133
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,357
Let's take the ship to Luffy's!

134
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,037
We'll grab him and get out of here!

135
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,880
Everyone move! Get on board!

136
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:07,770
Fire!

137
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:20,210
No!

138
00:09:20,293 --> 00:09:21,453
That's our escape ship!

139
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:27,200
Those bastards!

140
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:28,619
Now it's hopeless!

141
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:30,377
We're completely surrounded!

142
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:31,997
That ship was our only way out of here!

143
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,315
What are we gonna do?

144
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:42,940
Kokoro, Chimney, Kenpo, Chopper!

145
00:09:49,220 --> 00:09:50,300
No.

146
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:51,560
What now?

147
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,440
We've made it!

148
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:15,322
Out of the way!

149
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:16,600
Thank goodness!

150
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:27,150
Sanji!

151
00:10:27,233 --> 00:10:28,157
What the heck happened?

152
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:29,652
And where have you been?

153
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,330
Sorry.

154
00:10:32,413 --> 00:10:34,711
There was something I had to take care of.

155
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:37,020
Damn, this is bad.

156
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:38,957
We're pretty screwed right now.

157
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:42,717
I never thought they'd attack us
as long as we still had Robin here.

158
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:45,682
I was sure the bridge and
the ship would be safe.

159
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:47,759
That's far enough.

160
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:48,770
Surrender!

161
00:10:48,853 --> 00:10:50,517
Release the old lady and
the little gorilla arm.

162
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:52,482
There's no time for any of that.

163
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:54,520
Kermit, can't!

164
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:01,230
Fire.

165
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:09,657
Why does this always happen to us?

166
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:12,380
Go to them in the second kettlebell. Fire!

167
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:16,980
It was close!

168
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:18,200
Keep moving!

169
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:20,970
Fire!

170
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:23,377
Oh,

171
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:30,460
yeah.

172
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:35,650
Run!

173
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:02,710
Damn it!

174
00:12:02,793 --> 00:12:03,817
They took out the bridge!

175
00:12:03,900 --> 00:12:05,217
We're stuck on this column!

176
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:07,217
These bastards have got us cornered!

177
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:08,697
There's nothing else we can do!

178
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:09,697
We're surrounded!

179
00:12:09,780 --> 00:12:11,777
Then this is where we'll make our stand!

180
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:12,690
Let's fight!

181
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:13,603
Don't be stupid!

182
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:16,397
They'll just keep sending more
and more of those captains at us!

183
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:19,980
All ships, prepare to open
fire at the first column!

184
00:12:33,380 --> 00:12:35,460
All the Ganons take aim!

185
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:37,400
Eliminate Straw Hat Luffy!

186
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,080
Luffy!

187
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:53,980
He's in trouble.

188
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:56,440
You've got to do something. Crap.

189
00:12:56,820 --> 00:12:58,820
This is bad. No way!

190
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:02,800
No good at this distance.

191
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:06,300
All I can do is grab him
and throw him into the sea.

192
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:10,560
Bad news, you guys.

193
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:15,220
Straw Hat may have won the fight, but
now he's so weak, he can't get up.

194
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:16,401
He'll be killed.

195
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:19,917
Straw Hat! No! Straw Hat!

196
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,220
I don't give up!

197
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:23,740
Stand up, throw head!

198
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:27,260
Come on, stand up!

199
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:29,320
Pirate guy, run! Yeah!

200
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:31,250
Luffy!

201
00:13:31,333 --> 00:13:32,480
Hurry, move it!

202
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:35,577
Damn it, you've got to do
something right now, Luffy!

203
00:13:35,660 --> 00:13:36,490
Luffy!

204
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:37,510
Throw head!

205
00:13:37,780 --> 00:13:40,640
Come on, you can do it!

206
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:42,520
Throw head!

207
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:44,700
They don't give up!

208
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:49,180
No, I'm in trouble.

209
00:13:53,920 --> 00:13:56,020
There it is again. What?

210
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:00,037
Hey, you're trying to kill yourself?

211
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,320
Stop spacing out.

212
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:02,638
Now's not the time.

213
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:04,407
Whose voice is this, anyway?

214
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:08,010
That's right.

215
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:10,593
It's the same voice that I heard before.

216
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,889
What's going on over here?

217
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:23,610
What?

218
00:14:23,693 --> 00:14:25,280
Those voices? It's my guys.

219
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:27,857
No, that's not what
I'm talking about here.

220
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:29,137
I've heard it for a while.

221
00:14:29,220 --> 00:14:30,050
No!

222
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:44,080
What?

223
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:48,120
Look below.

224
00:14:59,220 --> 00:15:00,817
It's coming from...

225
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,100
over here. Below?

226
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:09,860
Who's that?

227
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:13,020
What the hell? That voice.

228
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:21,280
It says look below. Who does?

229
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:23,028
What are you talking about?

230
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:26,760
All ships open fire on the
first column in Stride, Luffy.

231
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:28,057
Commencing at five.

232
00:15:28,140 --> 00:15:29,100
No, Luppy!

233
00:15:38,580 --> 00:15:40,240
Jump in the sea!

234
00:15:42,540 --> 00:15:43,370
Four!

235
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:45,000
The sea!

236
00:15:46,860 --> 00:15:47,690
What's up?

237
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:51,006
Robin, can you still
throw Luppy into the sea?

238
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:52,010
Leave it to me.

239
00:15:52,093 --> 00:15:53,469
Are you trying to kill us?

240
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:57,293
Jump in the sea won't help a damn thing.

241
00:15:58,860 --> 00:16:00,420
We're gonna be safe!

242
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:04,300
She came to rescue us!
Jump! It'll be okay!

243
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:07,720
We still got one more friend here! Two!

244
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,320
Chopper! Did you see?

245
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:12,150
Yes!

246
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:17,600
Now, see and float.

247
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:25,510
One!

248
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:27,110
Delphinium!

249
00:16:29,140 --> 00:16:30,520
I'm moving!

250
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:32,320
Is Robin doing this?

251
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:35,780
To the sea!

252
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:38,120
To the sea!

253
00:16:38,780 --> 00:16:39,780
To the sea!

254
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:45,540
Jump!

255
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:46,840
Follow Luffy!

256
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:49,070
Go!

257
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:51,650
Go!

258
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:55,440
To the sea!

259
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:59,600
All of the pirates are
jumping into the sea! Ha!

260
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:02,477
There's no way those idiots
will survive in these waters!

261
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:03,457
They're done for!

262
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:06,540
Those Straw Hats are
completely out of their minds!

263
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,780
Let's go back, everyone!

264
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:42,520
Back to the seas of adventure.

265
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:49,280
Everyone, get on board the Mary!

266
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:54,650
Mary!

267
00:17:54,733 --> 00:17:55,563
Mary!

268
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:00,420
I came to get you!

269
00:18:02,860 --> 00:18:04,213
What are they thinking?

270
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:07,237
If they jump in the ocean,
they're just going to drown!

271
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:09,977
And they have Devil Fruit
users with them as well!

272
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:10,890
It's suicide!

273
00:18:11,940 --> 00:18:13,500
Hold on, look at that!

274
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:15,860
Is that their ship?

275
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:18,097
It's gotta be! See?

276
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:20,737
It even has a Straw Hat's fire flag on it!

277
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:23,879
How the hell did it stick
past all our battleships?!

278
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:46,456
I don't know who you are,
pal, but I sure owe you one.

279
00:18:53,180 --> 00:18:54,320
This is weird.

280
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:06,460
What's going on, Sanji?

281
00:19:06,580 --> 00:19:07,521
Something wrong?

282
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:09,780
Not wrong, just strange.

283
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:13,737
The rope ladder got dropped down, but
it doesn't look like anyone's here.

284
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:14,650
What?

285
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:15,770
Yay!

286
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:17,270
Yeah!

287
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:22,545
Seriously, can't you swim
on your own, brother?

288
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:25,240
Alrighty, up you go!

289
00:19:25,620 --> 00:19:27,460
Hope you enjoyed the ride!

290
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:30,020
Robin! Yoo-hoo!

291
00:19:30,620 --> 00:19:32,560
Leap into my arms, darling!

292
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:33,880
Over here!

293
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:41,160
We're on the ferry!

294
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:42,840
We're back on the ferry!

295
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,060
I love you, Barry!

296
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:46,660
I love you so much! Thank you!

297
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:50,090
Mary!

298
00:19:50,173 --> 00:19:53,620
My sweet Mary is still alive!

299
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:55,897
I don't understand!

300
00:19:55,980 --> 00:19:57,451
Why did she make it here?

301
00:19:57,880 --> 00:20:03,760
I wish I could give you a
hug, Mary, but I can't move!

302
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:05,670
This doesn't make sense.

303
00:20:05,753 --> 00:20:08,240
I saw the ship drop into the ocean myself.

304
00:20:22,300 --> 00:20:24,540
The question is, who sailed it here?

305
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:25,957
We'll figure it out later.

306
00:20:26,040 --> 00:20:26,870
Just get us out of here.

307
00:20:26,953 --> 00:20:27,783
Great.

308
00:20:27,866 --> 00:20:28,696
Let me think.

309
00:20:28,779 --> 00:20:29,609
Everyone ready?

310
00:20:29,692 --> 00:20:30,522
Sanji, get up!

311
00:20:30,605 --> 00:20:31,517
What are you doing?

312
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:33,894
Whatever you want me to do, Nami Sweet!

313
00:20:35,060 --> 00:20:36,400
That was a close one.

314
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:39,777
I thought those battleships were
going to blow me up for sure.

315
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:42,300
Hey, Robin, you saved me. Thanks a...

316
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:54,400
From now on, leave everything to us!

317
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:09,000
Luffy, everyone, thank you.

318
00:21:11,900 --> 00:21:13,820
Sure. Sure.

319
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:22,180
Don't worry about it.

320
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,937
That's nice, but save the sappy stuff!

321
00:21:30,020 --> 00:21:31,608
Till after we escape, okay?

322
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:34,440
You take that back, you heartless bastard!

323
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:35,960
Yeah, you bastard!

324
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:40,237
If we sit around, we're just gonna
end up dead and stupid I don't care!

325
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:42,400
Apologize to Robin! That's enough!

326
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:43,599
Both of you, stop!

327
00:21:43,820 --> 00:21:46,580
Hey, wait, Chopper, you're moving again.

328
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:48,710
Huh?

329
00:21:48,793 --> 00:21:51,047
Now that you mention
it, I guess I am moving.

330
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:53,280
I was afraid I'd never get better.

331
00:21:54,100 --> 00:21:56,280
Now apologize to Robin already!

332
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:59,800
Give up yet? No! Never!

333
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:02,080
Okay, let's go!

334
00:22:02,580 --> 00:22:04,700
You guys ready to move? Yeah!

335
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:08,057
Put it together, you idiots!

336
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:09,897
Are you just gonna stand
there and let them get away?

337
00:22:09,980 --> 00:22:13,857
If they're gonna escape anyway, we
might as well blow up Nico Rabbit, too!

338
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:14,770
But...

339
00:22:14,853 --> 00:22:16,887
but we're supposed to
capture her alive, sir.

340
00:22:17,100 --> 00:22:19,977
Tragic, I know, but that's
what Aokiji said to do.

341
00:22:20,060 --> 00:22:22,080
Now, all ships, prepare to fire!

342
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:24,860
Uh, Admiral Aokiji said that?

343
00:22:25,140 --> 00:22:26,840
All right, man, take aim!

344
00:22:27,260 --> 00:22:28,960
All ships, prepare to fire!

345
00:22:29,780 --> 00:22:31,480
Revenge, prepare to fire!

346
00:22:34,340 --> 00:22:37,657
Okay, so I lied, but that's
better than letting them get away.

347
00:22:37,740 --> 00:22:40,152
I'll make them pay for what they've done.

348
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:44,037
Can't you load those
cannonballs any faster?

349
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:45,077
Do you want them to get high?

350
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:47,520
Spawn them still alive, huh? That sucks.

351
00:22:47,860 --> 00:22:48,978
They're gonna fire!

352
00:22:49,180 --> 00:22:51,377
Catch the wind from
starboard and head east!

353
00:22:51,460 --> 00:22:53,157
We can't, we're completely surrounded.

354
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:56,297
All those big scary cannons and
they're aiming straight at us!

355
00:22:56,380 --> 00:22:59,997
In this range with that many ships,
there's no way they're gonna miss.

356
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:00,910
Fire!

357
00:23:04,860 --> 00:23:05,690
Help!

358
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:12,900
Wait, are they firing at each other?

359
00:23:13,220 --> 00:23:14,985
There ain't can't be that bad.

360
00:23:15,180 --> 00:23:16,200
What was that?

361
00:23:16,460 --> 00:23:17,557
Where the hell are you waiting?

362
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:18,577
Something's wrong.

363
00:23:18,660 --> 00:23:20,617
It's like the cannons just
did that on their own.

364
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:22,524
Don't make such stupid excuses.

365
00:23:24,200 --> 00:23:25,200
Change cars!

366
00:23:25,700 --> 00:23:26,760
It's too late!

367
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:37,097
They're coming straight at us!

368
00:23:37,180 --> 00:23:38,239
We're gonna crash!

369
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:42,600
This is madness!

370
00:23:42,880 --> 00:23:44,277
What the hell is going on here?

371
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:45,660
Look over there, sir!

372
00:23:49,460 --> 00:23:52,342
The Gates of Justice are
closing for some reason!

373
00:23:52,560 --> 00:23:54,317
The gate can't block the current anymore!

374
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:57,437
With these whirlpools around, we
won't be able to control the rudder!

375
00:23:57,520 --> 00:23:59,461
So that's why our aim was so bad!

376
00:23:59,560 --> 00:24:00,736
Don't get sucked in!

377
00:24:01,420 --> 00:24:03,832
This thing keeps going from back to work!

378
00:24:07,200 --> 00:24:08,917
Put out the fire! Quick!

379
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:10,765
We're gonna have to jump ship!

380
00:24:10,960 --> 00:24:11,790
We're finished!

381
00:24:11,873 --> 00:24:12,900
Those damn fools!

382
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:14,377
Why did they close the gate?

383
00:24:14,460 --> 00:24:16,537
Hurry the hell up and open it again!

384
00:24:16,620 --> 00:24:17,680
We can't, sir!

385
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:20,397
The operation lever is on
the bridge of hesitation!

386
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:21,656
It wasn't our fault!

387
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:24,277
That turned out better than I thought!

388
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:26,597
Sanji, is that what you
did while you were gone?

389
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:27,510
Mm-hmm.

390
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:32,024
I figured it'd take more than just
guts to get out of here alive.

391
00:24:36,820 --> 00:24:37,650
Bingo.

392
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:42,400
You'll like my hero forever, Sanji!

393
00:24:42,520 --> 00:24:43,991
Are you a genius or what?

394
00:24:44,080 --> 00:24:45,897
It's a little early to be kissing his ass.

395
00:24:45,980 --> 00:24:48,157
These whirlpools are
a problem for us, too.

396
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:49,070
Oh, great!

397
00:24:49,153 --> 00:24:49,983
Thanks a lot, Sanji!

398
00:24:50,066 --> 00:24:50,896
Would you shut up?

399
00:24:50,979 --> 00:24:51,840
It's not a problem.

400
00:24:52,260 --> 00:24:57,020
As long as we're together, there's no
sea that the Going Merry can't cross.

401
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:58,830
Right!

402
00:24:58,913 --> 00:25:01,580
You're so cool, Nami! That's right!

403
00:25:01,780 --> 00:25:03,015
Go for it, Navigator!

404
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:05,857
Just hold them off while
I find a path for us!

405
00:25:05,940 --> 00:25:06,770
No problem!

406
00:25:15,360 --> 00:25:18,860
One-sword-style, 36-caliber-6!

407
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:23,030
Dammit!

408
00:25:23,113 --> 00:25:24,257
Why do you idiots keep missing?

409
00:25:24,340 --> 00:25:25,340
It's right there!

410
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:28,817
We've got less a million cannons
firing at that stupid thing!

411
00:25:28,900 --> 00:25:30,429
It's just one little ship!

412
00:25:31,020 --> 00:25:32,317
They're coming your way, Luson!

413
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:35,680
I got him here! No way! I
missed one! Sanji, help!

414
00:25:36,260 --> 00:25:37,280
Pause, coot!

415
00:25:37,760 --> 00:25:40,280
Ah, guys, save some for me!

416
00:25:40,520 --> 00:25:41,932
I want to fight him too!

417
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:43,270
Really?

418
00:25:43,353 --> 00:25:45,200
Are you gonna squirm him to death?

419
00:25:45,820 --> 00:25:49,157
Hate to break it to you, Captain,
but I think this one is our battle.

420
00:25:49,240 --> 00:25:50,070
Take a nap.

421
00:25:50,153 --> 00:25:50,983
We've done it.

422
00:25:56,200 --> 00:25:57,820
You won't take a nap.

423
00:25:58,980 --> 00:26:01,340
I'm gonna make these guys go me.

424
00:26:02,300 --> 00:26:03,860
Just gotta get there.

425
00:26:06,140 --> 00:26:08,297
I'll give a medal to
anyone who can hit them!

426
00:26:08,380 --> 00:26:09,792
One shot is all attacks!

427
00:26:09,880 --> 00:26:13,240
All ships concentrate attacks
on their back deck! Fire!

428
00:26:17,140 --> 00:26:18,320
Shut up, Zoro!

429
00:26:18,620 --> 00:26:20,440
You can't tell me what to do!

430
00:26:34,740 --> 00:26:35,570
You're ready?

431
00:26:36,080 --> 00:26:36,910
Let's go.

432
00:26:39,080 --> 00:26:41,139
Uh-oh, I think they're coming back!

433
00:26:47,140 --> 00:26:49,097
You never let us down, huh, Captain?

434
00:26:49,180 --> 00:26:51,080
I guess we needed you after all.

435
00:26:51,300 --> 00:26:52,840
You people are monsters!

436
00:26:53,380 --> 00:26:54,210
Uh-huh.

437
00:26:59,680 --> 00:27:00,660
I've got it.

438
00:27:00,900 --> 00:27:02,260
The path to victory.

439
00:27:03,040 --> 00:27:04,628
Chopper, helm hard to port!

440
00:27:04,780 --> 00:27:05,610
Nine o 'clock!

441
00:27:05,693 --> 00:27:06,894
All right, you got it!

442
00:27:08,100 --> 00:27:10,017
They're pulling towards the waterfall!

443
00:27:10,100 --> 00:27:11,157
What should we do?

444
00:27:11,240 --> 00:27:12,300
Just shoot them!

445
00:27:12,600 --> 00:27:14,071
What the hell did you do?

446
00:27:14,280 --> 00:27:15,820
How hard can it be?

447
00:27:16,060 --> 00:27:17,297
Save that damn ship!

448
00:27:17,380 --> 00:27:19,657
They're riding the
current of the whirlpool.

449
00:27:19,740 --> 00:27:20,570
It's no use.

450
00:27:20,653 --> 00:27:22,440
We can't keep up. All right.

451
00:27:22,660 --> 00:27:24,200
I get to be useful, too.

452
00:27:24,540 --> 00:27:26,860
You can do it, reindeer dude. Yeah.

453
00:27:27,360 --> 00:27:28,360
Let's go.

454
00:27:29,280 --> 00:27:30,480
Full speed ahead.

455
00:27:34,020 --> 00:27:34,880
Damn it.

456
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:36,550
Damn it.

457
00:27:36,760 --> 00:27:37,800
Those bastards.

458
00:27:38,320 --> 00:27:40,261
I had the power of Vinny's lobby.

459
00:27:40,420 --> 00:27:41,800
The power of CP9.

460
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:44,480
I even had the power of a bastard call.

461
00:27:44,720 --> 00:27:47,297
They practically burned
the whole island down.

462
00:27:47,380 --> 00:27:51,500
And yet, even after all that,
even after all I've done,

463
00:27:51,780 --> 00:27:55,960
I can't take a single woman away
from a tiny band of riffraff!

464
00:27:57,240 --> 00:27:58,740
It's not fair!

465
00:28:24,780 --> 00:28:26,760
Chief Spandam!

466
00:28:38,020 --> 00:28:40,800
Please, someone help me!

467
00:28:43,380 --> 00:28:44,210
Clutch!

468
00:28:49,040 --> 00:28:50,922
Oh, jeez, Douglas, are you okay?

469
00:28:56,660 --> 00:28:58,000
Yeah! Go!

470
00:28:58,200 --> 00:29:00,037
Well, I guess that settles that.

471
00:29:00,120 --> 00:29:04,220
All right, Franky, it's time
to do your thing! You got it!

472
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:13,337
Get ready, kids, because
this is going to be wild.

473
00:29:13,420 --> 00:29:14,420
Bluff their hats!

474
00:29:14,660 --> 00:29:16,777
Don't let them get out of the portal!

475
00:29:16,860 --> 00:29:19,857
Just so you know, this might
bang up your ship a bit.

476
00:29:19,940 --> 00:29:21,080
Sorry about that.

477
00:29:21,800 --> 00:29:22,630
Kaido!

478
00:29:25,720 --> 00:29:26,740
Wait, what?

479
00:29:26,960 --> 00:29:28,580
The pirate ship is flying?

480
00:29:28,920 --> 00:29:30,802
How are we supposed to top that?

481
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:33,000
Our cannons can't reach that high.

482
00:29:34,100 --> 00:29:36,957
If you think that Mary's an
ordinary ship, then you're wrong.

483
00:29:37,040 --> 00:29:40,317
She's flown through the air once
and she can do it again no problem.

484
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:42,700
Special Attack Super Fox Star!

485
00:29:47,620 --> 00:29:48,880
It's a smokescreen!

486
00:29:55,180 --> 00:29:56,900
Put them pirates! Go!

487
00:29:57,320 --> 00:29:58,677
Don't let them get away!

488
00:29:58,760 --> 00:29:59,590
We can't, sir!

489
00:29:59,673 --> 00:30:01,517
It's taking all we've
got just to stay afloat!

490
00:30:01,600 --> 00:30:04,012
We gotta get out of this whirlpool first!

491
00:30:10,460 --> 00:30:11,290
Maintain fire!

492
00:30:11,373 --> 00:30:12,203
Don't stop!

493
00:30:42,560 --> 00:30:45,207
Looks like the straw
hats are safe and sound.

494
00:30:45,960 --> 00:30:46,790
Good.

495
00:30:46,873 --> 00:30:48,679
Now let's get the hell out of here.

496
00:30:59,580 --> 00:31:01,180
Let's go, Puppin' Tom!

497
00:31:01,460 --> 00:31:03,040
We're heading home!

498
00:31:10,780 --> 00:31:12,898
I didn't realize you were here, sir.

499
00:31:13,060 --> 00:31:15,137
We haven't given up the chase yet.

500
00:31:15,220 --> 00:31:17,340
I swear it won't end like this.

501
00:31:17,540 --> 00:31:20,000
We must maintain our dignity as the Navy.

502
00:31:20,380 --> 00:31:22,140
No, as the World Government.

503
00:31:22,440 --> 00:31:24,737
We'll bring down the
Straw Heads at any cost.

504
00:31:24,820 --> 00:31:26,817
Nico Robin is in the palm of our hand.

505
00:31:26,900 --> 00:31:29,537
We can't let her escape
again after all we've done.

506
00:31:29,620 --> 00:31:30,450
Admiral,

507
00:31:30,533 --> 00:31:34,097
allow us to call in reinforcements and
we'll overtake them as quickly as possible.

508
00:31:34,180 --> 00:31:35,780
Don't bother. But, sir,

509
00:31:35,960 --> 00:31:38,137
the force that we command
with a Buster Call

510
00:31:38,220 --> 00:31:40,926
is as powerful as an
entire nation's military.

511
00:31:41,300 --> 00:31:42,997
And yet, look at the state of our fleet.

512
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:45,668
Look at Annie's lobby
burning to the ground.

513
00:31:45,760 --> 00:31:47,819
The situation is obvious, isn't it?

514
00:31:48,320 --> 00:31:49,760
The day is lost, men.

515
00:31:50,260 --> 00:31:51,920
We've been utterly defeated.

516
00:31:53,100 --> 00:31:56,197
You sure you want to sit up
on top of that cheap head?

517
00:31:56,280 --> 00:31:57,162
Of course I do.

518
00:31:57,380 --> 00:31:58,909
That's the captain's seat.

519
00:31:59,140 --> 00:32:00,420
Well, there you go.

520
00:32:00,640 --> 00:32:01,816
Careful not to fall.

521
00:32:03,120 --> 00:32:03,950
Sure.

522
00:32:04,033 --> 00:32:05,217
Thanks for the help, Monster Granny.

523
00:32:05,300 --> 00:32:06,241
You're the best.

524
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:09,940
And thank you, Mary.

525
00:32:10,240 --> 00:32:12,377
We never would have made
it if you weren't there.

526
00:32:12,460 --> 00:32:15,040
I was pretty surprised when you showed up.

527
00:32:15,280 --> 00:32:18,697
But when I think about it, you've
always been there to protect us.

528
00:32:18,780 --> 00:32:20,540
We've always counted on you.

529
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:24,097
Anyway, I'm just happy you've
been part of the team, Mary.

530
00:32:24,180 --> 00:32:25,886
You're a good friend to have.

531
00:32:26,580 --> 00:32:28,404
I don't mean to spoil the mood.

532
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:32,220
Damn, you guys did some
crazy stuff back there.

533
00:32:32,460 --> 00:32:34,137
I don't think the
government's gonna let you

534
00:32:34,220 --> 00:32:37,620
off that easy after you burned
down their flag. Whatever.

535
00:32:38,420 --> 00:32:40,655
It doesn't feel like a big deal to me.

536
00:32:41,320 --> 00:32:43,837
The only reason I did
any of that was because

537
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:46,391
they took our friend and I wanted her back

538
00:32:47,180 --> 00:32:49,677
We couldn't have done what
we did without your help.

539
00:32:49,760 --> 00:32:50,642
So thanks a lot

540
00:32:51,460 --> 00:32:54,197
Well, like you said it wasn't
really that big a deal.

541
00:32:54,280 --> 00:32:55,809
I just do what I had to do

542
00:32:57,220 --> 00:33:03,180
Point is we're all together coming
back in one piece and this fight was

543
00:33:10,760 --> 00:33:11,590
Thank you.
